            "description": "Sundarijal is the gateway to Shivapuri Nagarjun National Park and the traditional starting point of the Helambu and Langtang treks. The trail to Chisapani is one of the most rewarding day hikes near Kathmandu, climbing steadily through dense forest along the Shivapuri ridge before opening up to panoramic Himalayan views.\n\nThe hike begins near the Sundarijal reservoir and water source, following stone-paved steps and forest trails through the national park. After a steep climb to Mulkharka village, the trail levels out somewhat as it winds through pine and rhododendron forest toward Chisapani. On a clear day, Chisapani offers sweeping views of the Langtang, Jugal, and Ganesh Himal ranges, along with a distant glimpse of the Kathmandu Valley below. Many trekkers use this route as Day 1 of the Helambu circuit, but it's equally popular as a demanding one-day round trip from the city.",
